# /etc/fw_env.config — where fw_printenv/fw_setenv (libubootenv-tool) find the
# redundant U-Boot environment pair.
#
# OWNER: RFCT-014 (RAUC integration). This is the single fw_env.config source
# in the tree; there is deliberately no os/rauc/fw_env.config.in to drift from
# it. It is rendered from os/boards/cx3576/board.env by os/rootfs/build-v2.sh, and
# os/rauc/render-config.sh asserts its contract (run on every bundle build):
# exactly two device lines, each addressing its UENV partition at offset 0 with
# size UENV_SIZE_BYTES, and those partition starts cross-checked against the
# byte offsets U-Boot's ENV_OFFSET/ENV_OFFSET_REDUND are pinned to.
#
# Two device lines is what marks the environment redundant to libubootenv. If
# only one side is configured redundant, every read from the other fails its
# CRC check.
#
# The pair is addressed by partition GUID rather than by a hardcoded
# /dev/mmcblk0 offset: the GUIDs are layout constants, the disk name is not.
#
# The environment addressed here exists on a v2 device — the image carries the
# uboot-mos variant, which has the redundant pair at UENV_A/B_OFFSET_BYTES, and
# os/mkimage-v2.sh refuses to assemble a v2 image around the debug variant.
#
# Two writers exist for this environment (RAUC slot marking and the first-boot
# machine-id oneshot), and libubootenv gives no cross-process locking, so their
# writes must never overlap.
#
# <device>                              <offset>  <env size>
/dev/disk/by-partuuid/@UENV_A_GUID@     0x0       @UENV_SIZE_HEX@
/dev/disk/by-partuuid/@UENV_B_GUID@     0x0       @UENV_SIZE_HEX@
